WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.980
MRI is a medical imaging device

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.700
commonly used to examine 
the soft tissues of the human body

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:10.420
Let's meet the machine.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.160
The key components are

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.200
Our bodies are made up of 60% water

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.440
and water is magnetic.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.520
Each of the billions

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.680
of water molecules inside us

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.400
consists of an oxygen atom

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.480
bonded to two hydrogen atoms.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.040
We know it as H2O.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.510
Small parts of the hydrogen atoms act as tiny magnets

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.880
and are very sensitive to magnetic fields.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.440
MRI stands for magnetic resonance imaging

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.710
and an MRI scanner is one of the
main diagnostic tools that doctors use

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.360
to examine inside our bodies.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.120
The first step in taking an MRI scan is to use a

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.240
big magnet to produce a unified magnetic
field around the patient.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.960
The gradient adjusts the magnetic field 
into smaller sections

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.640
of different magnetic strengths

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.680
to isolate specific body parts.

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:31.760
For example, the brain.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.880
Normally the water

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:42.000
molecules inside us are arranged randomly.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.620
But when we lie inside the magnetic field

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.000
most of our water
molecules move at the same rhythm or

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.920
frequency as the magnetic field.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.900
The ones that don't move along the magnetic field

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.560
are called low energy water molecules.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.060
To create an image of a body part,

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.600
for example the brain,

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.000
the machine focuses on the 
low energy water molecules.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.680
Radio waves move at the same
rhythm or frequency as the magnetic

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.880
fields in an MRI machine.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:16.960
By sending
radio waves that match or resonate with

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:22.540
the magnetic field the low energy water
molecules absorb the energy they need to

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:25.040
move alongside the magnetic field.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.260
When the machine stops emitting radio
waves the water molecules that had just

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:37.120
moved along the magnetic field release
the energy they had absorbed and go back

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.020
to their position.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.920
This movement is
detected by the MRI machine and the

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:50.350
signal is sent to a powerful computer
which uses imaging software to translate

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.480
the information into an image of the
body.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:55.900
By taking images of the body in

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.640
each section of the magnetic field the
machine produces a final three

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:05.880
dimensional image of the organ which
doctors can analyze to make a diagnosis.

